 "summary_en": "The county's own pages show that Vaasa Central Hospital has its own radiotherapy unit and a day ward for intravenous cancer drugs, and a 2025 local study found that Ostrobothnian lung cancer patients living 50 km from a hospital have worse survival. A Yle report from January 2026 says Vaasa Central Hospital is in the national low-dose CT screening pilot with stop-smoking support, but the checks did not accept it because the page does not name the county. I found no county decisions or lung-cancer-specific pathway or waiting-time figures.",
